# stack-enforcer skill

**Read and apply** `.cursor/skills/stack-enforcer/SKILL.md` before writing or committing this change.

Also read it when editing any `api/**/*.py` file and **adding or modifying a non-stdlib import**, or when the user mentions a third-party library (`openai`, `redis`, `langchain`, etc.).

Then read `docs/STACK_LOCK.md` §9 (forbidden imports) if not already in context.

Skill guidance wins over generic rules when both apply. Pre-commit hooks enforce regardless.
